Lab: Introduction to Microservice Architecture and Service Mesh Concepts
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Compare monolithic and microservice architectures and articulate their tradeoffs
Identify the key benefits and challenges of implementing microservices
Explore how OpenShift Service Mesh (Istio-based) addresses common microservice challenges
Interpret and document output from analysis scripts to build organizational recommendations
Configure and simulate service mesh traffic management patterns, including circuit breaking
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of software architecture concepts
Familiarity with containerization concepts (Docker basics)
Knowledge of REST APIs and HTTP protocols
Basic Linux command line experience
Familiarity with Kubernetes fundamentals
This lab runs entirely on a Linux machine with Python 3 installed. No cluster is required; all Kubernetes/Istio YAML is generated and reviewed locally as configuration artifacts. Verify your environment and install the one required Python dependency:

python3 --version
pip3 install --user requests
